<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis Botha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1862–1919</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis Botha was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> general and statesman. He helped found the Nieuwe Republiek in 1884, rose to command the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a> forces in the Second Boer War and afterwards worked for reconciliation with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. Prime Minister of the self-governing Transvaal Colony from 1907, he became the first Prime Minister of the Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> in 1910 and led it into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, conquering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-south-west-africa">German South West Africa</a> in 1915.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-botha.jpg" alt="Louis Botha" width="154" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louisbotha_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
